  "conclusion": "The Koriki v1.0 kernel is built from a product BSP: the public Actions S500 3.10 tree plus the libcidop prebuilt archive, older Actions BSP code and about 96 functions of device-maker code (USB stub/upgrade gadget, gadget descriptor sysfs, Bluetooth PCM audio, dwc3 overflow handling, LED/motor/audio board code tagged \"allen\", JTAG switching, alarm/forced-shutdown). That product tree was not found in any public repository searched. Koriki 1.0.3.1 build #40 comes from the same product tree with a different configuration. The closest public approximation is MiaUI's reconstruction, which recovers 29 of the 96 functions.",
